<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pampanga</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pampanga is a province in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luzon">Luzon</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> Bay, home of the Kapampangan people. Fertile and close to Manila, it supplied food and soldiers to the Spanish colony. During the British occupation of Manila in 1762–1764 the Spanish resistance under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-de-anda-y-salazar">Simón de Anda y Salazar</a> was based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bacolor">Bacolor</a> in Pampanga.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pampanga.jpg" alt="Pampanga" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lance Vanlewen · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crater_Lake_at_the_Mount_Pinatubo_Caldera_in_the_Philippines_(3).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
